## Overview
ElectroBlueprintKernel is the electronics domain engine for blueprint‑driven simulation.  
It models electronics as field‑organisms, supports cross‑domain physics coupling, and embeds full identity provenance.

## Architecture
- IdentityLayer  
- BlueprintIO (Parser, Serializer)  
- ModelLayer (ComponentLibrary, TopologyGraph, ConstraintSystem)  
- SimulationCore (FieldSolver, CircuitSolver, TimeStepper)  
- IntegrationBridge (DomainAdapters, EventBus)  
- ProvenanceEngine

## Purpose
Provide a unified electronics simulation kernel with:
- Field‑behavior modeling  
- Constraint prediction  
- Cross‑domain coupling  
- Identity‑encoded provenance